#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0543 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "dataset ADLBC. Columns STUDYID(Char), USUBJID(Char), PARAMCD(Char), AVALCA1N(Num), AVALCAT1(Char). ONE row: `CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1 | LOW`. Both halves of the pair are declared, so the second conjunct `not var_exists('AVALCAT1')` is FALSE and the rule is silent. The two wildcard patterns are disjoint, so this still yields exactly one expansion (y=1), not two."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVALCA1N type=Num
col AVALCAT1 type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 1 | LOW
